Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodologies

Part 9 — Hybrid Android Application Reverse Engineering Methodology (Beginner → Expert)

> Goal: Learn how to reverse engineer Android applications built from multiple technologies. Modern Android applications often combine Java, Kotlin, C/C++, Flutter, React Native, Unity, WebView, and third-party SDKs into one APK. Your objective is to reconstruct one coherent architecture spanning multiple runtimes rather than analyzing each technology in isolation.



> Core Principle:
Treat a hybrid APK as a distributed software system living inside one process (or several). Recover the boundaries first, then reconstruct how the runtimes cooperate.




