Stage 29 — Common Hybrid Investigation Mistakes

Avoid

Treating each runtime as an independent application.

Ignoring ownership transitions between technologies.

Following only one language's call graph.

Confusing framework initialization with application logic.

Overlooking shared state and persistence.

Ignoring thread and memory boundaries across runtimes.

Producing separate architectures instead of one integrated model.



---

Stage 30 — Hybrid APK Methodology Master Checklist

By the end of this stage, you should be able to:

✅ Identify and classify hybrid Android applications containing multiple runtimes.

✅ Reconstruct startup, execution, navigation, state, and communication across technology boundaries.

✅ Build unified call graphs, data-flow graphs, and architectural models spanning Java/Kotlin, native code, Flutter, React Native, Unity, WebView, and other frameworks.

✅ Track ownership of UI, state, memory, threads, persistence, networking, and plugins across runtimes.

✅ Validate reconstructed architecture through runtime observation and cross-runtime correlation.

✅ Produce a single, coherent architectural model that explains the entire application rather than isolated technology-specific views.



